INT. PARKING GARAGE LEVEL P4 - "SYNERGY SOCIAL" TENT - DAY

A pop-up gazebo between two oil stains. Banner: MANDATORY FUN. Folding table. Sheet cake, sweating.

DESMOND PRUITT, 50s, lanyard heavy as a medal. Clipboard. Smiles at nobody.

ANOUK VAN DER BERG, 30s, auditor. Stabs cake with a plastic knife. Doesn't look up.

TAKESHI ONO, 20s, intern. Hoodie. Holding a balloon he was told to hold.

LOLA FERREIRA, 40s, HR. Headset. Always mid-sentence.

DESMOND
Welcome, team. Who's having fun?

Silence. A car alarm chirps two floors up.

DESMOND (CONT'D)
Let's circle back on that.

ANOUK
Is this billable?

LOLA
(into headset)
No, I'm listening, I'm just also here.

Takeshi's balloon drifts toward a sprinkler. He catches it. Desmond and Takeshi both freeze.

DESMOND
That's a safety balloon.

TAKESHI
It's a regular balloon.

DESMOND
Compliance says safety.

Anouk slides a slice of cake onto a paper plate. Lola and Desmond reach for it at once. They fight over the plate. Frosting on a lanyard.

LOLA
Wellness incident. I'm logging it.

ANOUK
You're the logger.

LOLA
I'm logging that I logged.

A forklift beeps in reverse. Everyone looks. It goes nowhere.

TAKESHI
Do we get to leave?

DESMOND
Leave is a strong word.

ANOUK
Ten minutes of fun, then my report.

DESMOND
What's in the report?

ANOUK
Cake. Mostly cake.

The group scatters toward their cars, then stops. Nobody has the right keys. They drift back to the table.

LOLA
(whispering)
Same time next quarter.

Desmond raises the clipboard like a toast. Nobody joins him.
